#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Workbench harness updater: catalogue checks and session-safe updates.

The updater never guesses a package source.  Each supported harness has one
measured installation path below.  In-place package managers are blocked while
a program of that harness runs on this machine (measured on the process table,
2026-10-10); versioned native/Homebrew/mise paths may switch while an old process
keeps running.  Every `anwenden` run ends with `wb-modelle entdecken`: new models
are discovered, probed with one short call and reported.

Model engines (Ollama, Splash) are kept only after their probe passed: the old
keg stays until then and is restored otherwise, with a report to leitung.  A
main-version jump of an engine is only noted; `anwenden <engine> --freigabe`
applies it, again behind the probe (Splash 1.0 -> 1.3 on 2026-10-10 stopped
loading the default model after an unprobed app-start run).
"""

